     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Deploying mfa:admin alone is enough, and with no controls the attack succeeds, so the minimum is 1. Without defences: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. Every route to exfiltration needs stolen_dbadmin. That comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, obtainable only through auth_dc or auth_adfs, and both require NOT mfa_admin. So mfa:admin blocks every path to exfiltration.\"}"
